# Grothendieck tribute — Part 53: arrow form of the topology generated by a precoverage

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Extension Phase 5 (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-52 established the fundamentals: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, sheaf bases, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicity, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Čech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limit, Kan extensions, adjunctions,
monads, equivalences, monoidal categories, the Grothendieck construction,
direct/exceptional image, the arrow form of the covering, the coherence
laws of the pullback pseudo-functor, the indexed lattice laws, the arrow
form of dense, extremal, pushforward-pullback adjunction, bind,
pretopology-generated, induced-topology, cover-preserving functors, the
composition laws of these functors, and the topology generated by a
coverage in the sense of `Coverage`.

This part applies the "arrow form" leitmotiv to the **topology generated
by a precoverage** (`Precoverage.toGrothendieck`). Mathlib provides at the
point level `Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff`:
`S ∈ J.toGrothendieck X ↔ Saturate J X S`, but **no law connects it to the
arrow form** `J.Covers`. We fill the gap with five proper theorems —
identical structure to Part 52 but at a more primitive level, since
`Precoverage.Saturate` (4 constructors: `of`, `top`, `pullback`, `transitive`)
is more primitive than `Coverage.Saturate` (3 constructors: pullback
stability being integrated in the very notion of `Coverage`):

  - `covers_iff_toGrothendieck` (central): for `J : Precoverage C`,
    `J.toGrothendieck.Covers S f ↔ Saturate J Y (S.pullback f)` — direct
    bridge between the arrow form and the inductive extension `Saturate`,
    via `covers_iff` and `Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff`. This is the
    **natural law** at the precoverage stage.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_of_of` (particular case): if `R ∈ J X` is a
    precoverage, then the sieve it generates covers the identity:
    `J.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) (𝟙 X)` — the forward
    direction of `Saturate.of`.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_top` (particular case): the trivial cover
    `⊤` covers any arrow: `J.toGrothendieck.Covers ⊤ f`. Fall-out of the
    constructor `Saturate.top` via `covers_iff` and `mem_toGrothendieck_iff`.
  - `covers_of_mem_toGrothendieck` (passage via `Sieve.generate`): if
    `R` is a precoverage, then `J.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) f`
    — for any arrow `f : Y ⟶ X`, the cover descends one notch via pullback
    stability (`Saturate.pullback`) which here appears as an **inductive
    constructor** (vs. axiom in `Coverage`).
  - `covers_iff_pullback_toGrothendieck` (particular case on identity):
    `J.toGrothendieck.Covers S (𝟙 X) ↔ S ∈ J.toGrothendieck X` — the
    point-level fall-out, via `Sieve.pullback_id` + `covers_iff`.

Each proof is a **real tactical proof** (DEEP vein): Mathlib axioms
(`GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff`, `Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff`,
`Precoverage.Saturate.pullback`, `Precoverage.Saturate.top`, `Precoverage.Saturate.of`,
`Sieve.pullback_id`, `Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck`) plus the
definition `Precoverage.toGrothendieck`. No proof is a re-export or an
unfold.

EPIC #1646, Phase 5 (#2159). All `sorry`s eliminated at creation.

